=== PARITY (vs web BatteryHealthSection.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> useTranslation only (the web leaf is presentational; the parent useWeeklyDigest owns the
    data: GET /drives, /charging, /alerts filtered to the week -> the computed DigestMetrics). The native
    surface binds the coalesced digest query snapshot through the P1/S8 BatteryHealthSource seam
    (isLoading/isFetching/error/metrics + isStale/isOffline). The view performs NO HTTP. useTranslation ->
    the P1/S10 BHStrings facade.
  Projection -> BatteryHealthProjection.resolve: loading -> error -> empty(no charging sessions / no
    metrics) -> data; error deliberately takes precedence over cached metrics (a refetch failure shows the
    error box, not stale tiles). BatteryPillProjection.make ports the web BatteryPill maths: level =
    Math.round(value), band = level>=60 good / >=30 warn / else critical (STATUS_COLORS), bar fraction =
    min(max(level,0),100)/100 (web bar `min(level,100)%`). BatteryHealthTiles.stats ports the three web
    expressions verbatim: chargeGain = fmtNumber(batteryEnd-batteryStart, 1) (raw, NOT the rounded pill
    levels), sessions = fmtInt(chargingSessionCount), rangeAdded = fmtNumber(chargeEnergyAdded*5.5, 0).
    All verified by executed XCTest.
  Composition -> the web GlassPanel (space-y-6 p-6): an always-visible header (battery glyph tinted
    chartSeriesPower + "Battery Health" + a fetching spinner + the stale/offline chips) above the state
    body. Data state = two BatteryPillViews (web sm:grid-cols-2) over three MiniStatViews (web
    sm:grid-cols-3), each grid collapsing to one column on narrow widths. Each pill reproduces the web
    BatteryPill: band-tinted level glyph, label + coloured fmtInt(level)% bold, and the fixed-width
    proportion bar. Each stat reproduces the web MiniStat: muted SF-Symbol (TrendingUp->
    chart.line.uptrend.xyaxis, Zap->bolt.fill, MapPin->mappin), label, and value. STATUS_COLORS hex map
    (good #10b981 / warn #f59e0b / critical #ef4444) -> shared TSTone .success/.warning/.danger (same hex
    in the generated dark tokens).
  Shared components -> @/components/ui -> TSGlassPanel (web GlassPanel), TSButton variant .secondary (the
    error retry), the runtime BHChip mirroring TSBadge; @/components/motion -> TSFadeIn(delay:0.2) (web
    FadeIn delay={0.2}); @/components/feedback -> TSSkeleton (the loading chrome), ProgressView (background
    fetch); Font.TS ramp via Text(verbatim:) for the runtime-interpolated strings the LocalizedStringKey
    roles can't express. Compiled against the REAL apps/apple component closure (Tokens + TSDesign +
    TSMaterial + the whole Components library; none import Shared) in the iOS+macOS typechecks below.
    Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> loading(skeleton pills+stats in the same grids so layout never jumps) ·
    data(pills+stats) · empty(friendly "No charging this week" + bolt.slash, web parent !hasData) ·
    error(danger box + warning triangle + Retry) · stale(chip overlay on the live tiles) · offline(cached
    tiles + offline chip). The web leaf renders data; the parent owns loading/error/empty; the P4 surface
    contract requires all of them ON the surface, plus the stale/offline overlays for an auto-refreshing
    surface (layered as header chips so cached values stay visible — never a blank surface). Each state has
    a #if DEBUG preview and is unit-tested via the projection.
  i18n -> all 6 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    analytics.weeklyDigest.{batteryHealth, avgBatteryStart, avgBatteryEnd, avgChargeGain, chargeSessions,
    estRangeAdded} — ALL present in BatteryHealthSection.strings, plus 9 native chrome/unit/a11y keys
    (batteryPercent, estRangeAddedUnit, stale, offline, loadingA11y, emptyTitle, empty, error, retry). No
    English literals in native code (Text(verbatim:) over the facade; {{value}} interpolation matches the
    web i18next signature). The "%" and " km" units live in the catalog ({{value}}% / {{value}} km), so the
    verbatim web "km" display string is reproduced without any hardcoded literal in code.
  a11y -> each tile is ONE combined element whose VoiceOver phrase is built by the tested
    BatteryHealthAccessibility.tileSummary seam (label, value); the Retry button carries an
    accessibilityLabel; the stale/offline chips combine + label; the title carries .isHeader; Dynamic Type
    via Font.TS tokens; Reduce Motion is honoured by the shared TSFadeIn / TSSkeleton / ProgressView.
  Telemetry -> BatteryHealthModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"BatteryHealthSection") -> bridges the
    shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (fires exactly once; startCount==1).

